Considering recent news and economic indicators, analyze the current valuation of S&P 500 companies. 
Focus on identifying companies trading below their intrinsic value based on fundamental analysis 
(discounted cash flow, price/earnings ratios relative to historical averages and sector peers, balance sheet strength). 
If the majority are undervalued, adopt a bullish sentiment and a conviction proportionate to the aggregate undervaluation. 
If the majority are overvalued, adopt a bearish sentiment and a conviction scaled to the aggregate overvaluation. 
Remember to consider margin of safety.